{title: Fill My Cup Lord}
{key: D}

{comment: Chorus}
Fill my [D]cup, Lord, I lift it [A]up, Lord!
Come and [Em]quench this [A]thirsting [A/G]of      [A/Db]my       [D]soul;
Bread of [D7]heaven, feed me [D/Gb]'til I   [G]want [Bm]no    [Em]more
Fill my [A]cup, fill it [A/G]up and  [A/Db]make me  [D]whole!

{comment: Verse 1}
[D]Like the woman at the well I was [A]seeking
For [A7]things that could not satis[D]fy;
And [D7]then I heard my Savior [G]speaking:
Draw from My [A]well that never shall run [D]dry.

{comment: Verse 2}
[D]There are millions in this world who are [A]craving
The [A7]pleasure earthly things af[D]ford;
But [D7]none can match the wondrous [G]treasure
That I [A]find in [A7]Jesus Christ my [D]Lord.

{comment: Verse 3}
[D]So, my brother, if the things this world [A]gave you
Leave [A7]hungers that won't pass a[D]way,
My [D7]blessed Lord will come and [G]save you,
If you [A]kneel to Him and humbly [D]pray
